MID_SE_Buc_Jas_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_C_001: Ngah! Hyah!
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_C_002: Jasmine, do you have a moment? There's something\nI've wanted to ask you.
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_C_003: Buccar. Uh, sure. What's up?
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_C_004: It's the way you fight... Something about it reminds\nme of someone with a knight's training.
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_C_005: Did you serve a house somewhere before you\nbecame a mercenary?
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_C_006: Good eye! Yeah, I did.
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_C_007: I served a regional lord in Arago. Did a stint in the\nroyal army for a time too.
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_C_008: Arago? I have to ask—were you involved in the\nCydonia Massacre?
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_C_009: Well, I was just a regular soldier at that time, so\nI went where I was told.
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_C_010: It was over before they could put up a proper fight.\nThe lord I served was of a similar standing.
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_C_011: He was a noble, sure, but a minor one. His house had\nno real presence in national politics.
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_C_012: After King Hasdrubal was killed, my lord's house\nwas sucked into the chaos. They got crushed.
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_C_013: My fighting skills were all I had left after that.\nThat's how I ended up a mercenary.
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_C_014: I see. It sounds like we've both been through a lot.
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_C_015: The Cydonia Massacre has taken each of our lords\nfrom us.
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_C_016: Seems we have some common ground. Perhaps we'll\nget along well.
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_C_017: Hahaha! I didn't expect you to say that. But hey,\nyou're probably right.
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_C_018: Alright then. In that case, we'll begin your training\nimmediately.
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_C_019: Huh? What are you talking about?
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_C_020: I've thought about it since I saw you fight... You've\nmuddied a knight's technique with other moves.
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_C_021: Sure, I started mixing in moves I learned as a\nmercenary. Made up my own fighting style.
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_C_022: Heh. Half this. Half that. It's intolerable. I want to\ntrain you properly, from the beginning.
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_C_023: We will start with the basic stance! Get in position,\nand I'll tell you exactly how you're doing it wrong!
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_C_024: Slow down, Bucko. Yeah, I don't like where this\nis going.
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_B_001: Left yourself open! Now you're mine! Hyah!
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_B_002: All taken care of! But there's more coming. Don't\nlet up, Buccar!
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_B_003: I know what to do! Take that!
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_B_004: Ahh... All clear, finally.
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_B_005: You fought with great skill. Hmm... So that is your\nself-made fighting style, is it?
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_B_006: The foundation is strong. I can tell your stances were\ndrilled into you when you trained as a knight.
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_B_007: I also noticed you were quick to assess each enemy\nand then deftly exploit their missteps.
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_B_008: You have fused a knight's technique with a\nmercenary's. It is a powerful combination.
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_B_009: I guess. But you're making it sound way more\ncomplicated than it is.
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_B_010: This is just how I do my work. And I won't change\nto suit anyone else.
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_B_011: This "powerful combination" is how I've managed to\nsurvive, and I'm proud of it.
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_B_012: Is now the part where you tell me to fight more like\na knight or something?
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_B_013: Not at all. How could I say something like that after\nyour performance in battle?
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_B_014: Though, if you'd been my student back in the day,\nI'd have whipped you into shape without hesitation.
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_B_015: Heh. You're so hardheaded. Why does it matter if\nyou or anyone fights like a proper knight?
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_B_016: I have my dignity, just as you have your pride.
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_B_017: I've spent a lifetime honing my skills as a knight,\nyou see.
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_B_018: There are some things I am unwilling to change.\nThe same goes for you, it seems.
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_B_019: I get it. You've got your way, and I've got mine.
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_B_020: Our fighting styles really are a way of life for us,\naren't they?
MID_SE_Buc_Jas_B_021: A way of life... Yes. All we can do is follow our\nown path and fight to the very end.